KG42.register("rules-25327bad4b67e6b27e97e619",{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R007","paper":"31-coalition_formation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"Local balancing of aggregate supplied and received battery energy is used to calculate the state-2 charging and discharging prices. Scope: State-2 battery-energy trading within the considered P2P network. Condition: Using aggregate energy-response expressions (15) and (16) and the assumed charging/discharging-price relation (17). Government tax and subscription-fee payment obligations are captured through β in the charging/discharging-price relationship. Scope: P2P battery charging/discharging-price relationship. Condition: When the grid transmission line is used for P2P trading. Set the P2P discharging price to the average of p_b(t) and p_s(t), and set the charging price to (1+β) times the discharging price. Scope: Initial P2P price setting in Algorithm 1 at each time slot. The trading price should reflect the associated battery degradation cost and provide enough incentive to make putting the battery into the market beneficial. Scope: Prices for battery-energy trading in the proposed P2P scheme. Condition: When a prosumer wishes to charge or discharge its battery for P2P trading.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E002","source":"settlement.payment","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E30"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Initial P2P price setting in Algorithm 1 at each time slot. | P2P battery charging/discharging-price relationship. | Prices for battery-energy trading in the proposed P2P scheme. | State-2 battery-energy trading within the considered P2P network.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x-Ed","symbol":"E_d(t)","meaning":"Total energy discharged by the provider set in state-2 P2P trading at time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Time-indexed aggregate battery-energy quantity for t = 1,...,T; sign is not separately stated in the supplied balance sentence.","unit":"energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x-Ec","symbol":"E_c(t)","meaning":"Total energy charged by the receiver set in state-2 P2P trading at time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Time-indexed aggregate battery-energy quantity for t = 1,...,T; sign is not separately stated in the supplied balance sentence.","unit":"energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pd","symbol":"p_d(t)","meaning":"P2P discharging price per unit of energy at time slot t set in Algorithm 1.","kind":"operational","domain":"t = 1,...,T; per-unit-energy price, sign not separately specified in the supplied pricing statements.","unit":"per unit energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E30"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pc","symbol":"p_c(t)","meaning":"P2P charging price per unit of energy at time slot t set in Algorithm 1.","kind":"operational","domain":"t = 1,...,T; per-unit-energy price, sign not separately specified in the supplied pricing statements.","unit":"per unit energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E30"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pd-s2","symbol":"p_{d,s2}(t)","meaning":"State-2 P2P discharging price per unit of energy calculated from local aggregate battery-energy balance, as in Eq. (18).","kind":"operational","domain":"t = 1,...,T; per-unit-energy price, sign not separately specified in the supplied pricing statements.","unit":"per unit energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pc-s2","symbol":"p_{c,s2}(t)","meaning":"State-2 P2P charging price per unit of energy derived from the discharging price by the markup relation, as in Eq. (17)/(19).","kind":"operational","domain":"t = 1,...,T; per-unit-energy price, sign not separately specified in the supplied pricing statements.","unit":"per unit energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E33"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-pb","symbol":"p_b(t)","meaning":"Mid-market buying price per unit of energy at time slot t, used as an input to the initial P2P price setting.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"unspecified time-indexed value"},"unit":"per unit energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-ps","symbol":"p_s(t)","meaning":"Mid-market selling price per unit of energy at time slot t, used as an input to the initial P2P price setting.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"unspecified time-indexed value"},"unit":"per unit energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-beta","symbol":"β","meaning":"Positive markup parameter in the charging/discharging price relationship, capturing government tax and subscription-fee obligations for grid transmission-line use.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"β > 0"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-pl","symbol":"p_l","meaning":"Battery degradation cost per kWh used in the state-2 price expression.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"unspecified numeric value"},"unit":"per kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-alpha-c","symbol":"α_c","meaning":"Common charging satisfaction parameter for receivers, assumed equal to α_{m,c} for all m in the receiver set L.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"common value assumed; numerical value unspecified"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-alpha-d","symbol":"α_d","meaning":"Common discharging satisfaction parameter for providers, assumed equal to α_{n,d} for all n in the provider set K.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"common value assumed; numerical value unspecified"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-k","symbol":"k","meaning":"Scaling factor in the battery utility functions, with 0 \u003c k ≤ 1.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"0 \u003c k ≤ 1"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-K","symbol":"K","meaning":"Total number of providers in coalition 2 / set K.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"K; exact value unspecified"},"unit":"count","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-L","symbol":"L","meaning":"Total number of receivers in coalition 2 / set L.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"L; exact value unspecified"},"unit":"count","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-s-n-d","symbol":"s_{n,d}(t)","meaning":"Battery-state quantity for provider n as printed in Eq. (18); no separate definition is supplied in the provided pages.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"as printed in Eq. (18); value unspecified"},"unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g02-E28","v141-b-g02-E32"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-b-m-c","symbol":"b_{m,c}(t)","meaning":"Battery capacity/state quantity for receiver m as printed in Eq. (18); no separate definition is supplied in the provided pages.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"as printed in Eq. (18); value unspecified"},"unit":null,"indices":["m","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-s-m-c","symbol":"s_{m,c}(t)","meaning":"Battery-state quantity for receiver m as printed in Eq. (18); no separate definition is supplied in the provided pages.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"as printed in Eq. (18); value unspecified"},"unit":null,"indices":["m","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Local balancing of aggregate supplied and received battery energy is used to calculate the state-2 charging and discharging prices. Scope: State-2 battery-energy trading within the considered P2P network. Condition: Using aggregate energy-response expressions (15) and (16) and the assumed charging/discharging-price relation (17).","expression":"E_d(t) = E_c(t); p_{d,s2}(t) = [p_l(α_c K - α_d L) - k(α_c Σ_{n=1}^{K} s_{n,d}(t) - α_d Σ_{m=1}^{L}(b_{m,c}(t) - s_{m,c}(t)))] / [α_c K + α_d(1 + β)L]; p_{c,s2}(t) = (1 + β) p_{d,s2}(t)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R007-x-Ed","v141-c-R007-x-Ec","v141-c-R007-x-pd-s2","v141-c-R007-x-pc-s2"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R007-theta-pl","v141-c-R007-theta-alpha-c","v141-c-R007-theta-alpha-d","v141-c-R007-theta-k","v141-c-R007-theta-K","v141-c-R007-theta-L","v141-c-R007-theta-s-n-d","v141-c-R007-theta-b-m-c","v141-c-R007-theta-s-m-c","v141-c-R007-theta-beta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E31","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Government tax and subscription-fee payment obligations are captured through β in the charging/discharging-price relationship. Scope: P2P battery charging/discharging-price relationship. Condition: When the grid transmission line is used for P2P trading.","expression":"p_c(t) = (1 + β) p_d(t); β > 0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R007-x-pc","v141-c-R007-x-pd"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R007-theta-beta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E30"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Set the P2P discharging price to the average of p_b(t) and p_s(t), and set the charging price to (1+β) times the discharging price. Scope: Initial P2P price setting in Algorithm 1 at each time slot.","expression":"p_d(t) = (p_b(t) + p_s(t)) / 2; p_c(t) = (1 + β) p_d(t)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R007-x-pd","v141-c-R007-x-pc"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R007-theta-pb","v141-c-R007-theta-ps","v141-c-R007-theta-beta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The trading price should reflect the associated battery degradation cost and provide enough incentive to make putting the battery into the market beneficial. Scope: Prices for battery-energy trading in the proposed P2P scheme. Condition: When a prosumer wishes to charge or discharge its battery for P2P trading.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E26"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3 Coalition formation algorithm","anchor_text":"players over , i.e., { 1, 2 , … , }i ▷ , as per the Pareto order in Definition 1. The reorganisation","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1. Algorithm to form a stable coalition structure for P2P trading. 1: for time slot $t=1$ to $T$ do 2: Set P2P discharge price $p_d(t)=\\frac{p_b(t)+p_s(t)}{2}$. 3: Set P2P charge price $p_c(t)=(1+\\beta)p_d(t)$. 4: for Each prosumer $n\\in\\mathcal{N}$ do"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3 Coalition formation algorithm","anchor_text":"tion structure, there is no coalition of prosumers who do not charge/ discharge batteries with who w","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Here, it is important to note that, in the proposed coalition formation structure, there is no coalition of prosumers who do not charge/discharge batteries with who will discharge/charge. This is due to the fact that, as the proposed scheme is designed, the charging and discharging price needs to satisfy the conditions explained in Table 2, where the threshold price $p_{n,c}(t)$ and $p_{n,d}(t)$ include the associated charging and discharging degradation cost of batteries. The motivation behind the choice of such prices is the fact that when a prosumer may want its battery to be charged or discharged for trading in the peer-to-peer market, the trading price should reflect the associated battery degradation cost due to charging and discharging, and at the same time, have enough incentive to make the price beneficial for prosumers to put their batteries into the market. Now, prosumers who participate in peer-to-peer trading market without battery do not need to consider such degradation cost and therefore the trading price does not include the additional item to compensate for the cost of battery degradation [39,51]. Given this context, as the proposed model is designed, these prices will always fall within the case 3 of Table 2, which subsequently removes the possibility of a trade between prosumers who do not charge/discharge batteries with prosumers who will discharge/charge at the same time."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"W. Tushar, et al. coalition can be expressed by (2 L L m = 1 (bm , c ( t ) sm, c ( t )) ( pl + pc ( ","equation_id":"16-17","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Now, let us consider that the P2P charging price $p_c(t)$ and discharging price $p_d(t)$ per unit of energy are related to one another via [52] $p_c(t)=(1+\\beta)p_d(t)$ (17), where $\\beta>0$. The relationship in (17) is motivated by the fact that a prosumer needs to pay the government tax and a subscription fee, captured via $\\beta$, for using the transmission line provide by the grid for P2P purpose."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E31","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"prosumer needs to pay the government tax and a subscription fee, ca captured via , for using the tra","equation_id":"18-19","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Now, the flow of energy for charging and discharging batteries via P2P establishes that the total energy charged by the receivers batteries should be equal to the total energy discharged by the providers in $\\mathcal{V}$, i.e., $E_d(t)=E_c(t)$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E32","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"prosumer needs to pay the government tax and a subscription fee, ca captured via , for using the tra","equation_id":"18-19","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To this end, by equating (15) and (16) and replacing the value of $p_c(t)$ with $p_d(t)$ from (17), the trading prices $p_c(t)$ and $p_d(t)$ for prosumers at state 2 can be calculated as: $p_{d,s2}(t)=\\frac{p_l(\\alpha_c K-\\alpha_d L)-k\\left(\\alpha_c\\sum_{n=1}^{K}s_{n,d}(t)-\\alpha_d\\sum_{m=1}^{L}(b_{m,c}(t)-s_{m,c}(t))\\right)}{\\alpha_c K+\\alpha_d(1+\\beta)L}$ (18)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E011","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.2 Utility of a prosumer at state 2","anchor_text":"thefact that the benefit to a prosumer for charging its battery even- wpr tually gets saturated with","equation_id":"5","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We note that the utility that a prosumer obtains from charging its battery can be defined as the sum of the relevant cost and the benefit of charging. Benefit of charging can be captured by using a utility function with decreasing marginal benefit [34,44,45]. Such a property refers to the fact that the benefit to a prosumer for charging its battery eventually gets saturated with charging as the SoC s_n(t) of the battery becomes close to its available capacity b_{n,c}(t) = b_n - s_n(t).\nTo this end, we consider the utility of a state 2 prosumer n for charging its battery as:\nU_{n,c}(t) = k\\left[b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right] - (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t). (5)\nIn (5), the term \\left(b_{n,c}(t)e_{n,c}(t) - \\frac{1}{2}\\alpha_n e_{n,c}(t)^2\\right) refers to the benefit of charging, 0 \u003c k \\le 1 is a scaling factor, and (p_l + p_c(t))e_{n,c}(t) is the cost of charging. Here, p_l is the degradation cost per kWh of the battery [46], p_c(t) is the price per unit of charging energy e_{n,c}(t) \\le E_{chr,dis} (where, E_{chr,dis} is the rated charging/discharging rate of the battery), and \\alpha_n > 0 is the satisfaction parameter of prosumer n [44]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3 Coalition formation algorithm","anchor_text":"in 25: Total demand from is mL = 1 em, c t( ) . 26: if nK= 1 en, d (t ) > mL = 1 em, c (t ) then he ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"24: Total available energy from $\\mathcal{K}$ is $\\sum_{n=1}^{K}e_{n,d}(t)$. 25: Total demand from $\\mathcal{L}$ is $\\sum_{m=1}^{L}e_{m,c}(t)$. 26: if $\\sum_{n=1}^{K}e_{n,d}(t)>\\sum_{m=1}^{L}e_{m,c}(t)$ then 27: All prosumers in $\\mathcal{L}$ finally chooses type 2. 28: Calculate excess energy $E_{ex,s}(t)=\\sum_{n=1}^{K}e_{n,d}(t)-\\sum_{m=1}^{L}e_{m,c}(t)$. 29: Set $e_{n,d}(t)=e_{n,d}(t)-\\min(e_{n,d}(t),\\frac{E_{ex,s}(t)}{K}), \\forall n\\in\\mathcal{K}$. 30: if $e_{n,d}(t)>0$ then 31: Prosumer $n$ decides to be in type 2. 32: else 33: Prosumer $n$ decides to be in $\\mathcal{W}$. 34: end if"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E21","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3 Coalition formation algorithm","anchor_text":"in 25: Total demand from is mL = 1 em, c t( ) . 26: if nK= 1 en, d (t ) > mL = 1 em, c (t ) then he ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"35: else if $\\sum_{n=1}^{K}e_{n,d}(t)\u003c\\sum_{m=1}^{L}e_{m,c}(t)$ 36: All prosumers in $\\mathcal{K}$ finally chooses type 2. 37: Calculate excess demand $E_{ex,d}(t)=\\sum_{m=1}^{L}e_{m,c}(t)-\\sum_{n=1}^{K}e_{n,d}(t)$. 38: Set $e_{m,c}(t)=e_{m,c}(t)-\\min(e_{m,c}(t),\\frac{E_{ex,d}(t)}{L}), \\forall m\\in\\mathcal{L}$. 39: if $e_{m,c}(t)>0$ then 40: Prosumer $n$ decides to be in $\\mathcal{V}$. 41: else 42: Prosumer $n$ decides to be in $\\mathcal{W}$. 43: end if"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"y, p g y p e- not charge/discharge batteries with prosumers who will discharge/ A charge at the same","equation_id":"14","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The total energy supplied by $K$ providers for the P2P trading is $E_d(t)=\\sum_{n=1}^{K}e_{n,d}(t)=\\sum_{n=1}^{K}\\frac{1}{k\\alpha_{n,d}}\\left(k s_{n,d}(t)-p_l+p_d(t)\\right)$ (14)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E28","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"e/ he K K 1 s- Ed ( t ) = n = 1 en, d ( t ) = n = 1 k n, d ( ksn, d ( t ) pl + pd ( t )). (14) 2, ed","equation_id":"15","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Without loss of generality, it can be considered that $\\alpha_{n,d}=\\alpha_d, \\forall n\\in\\mathcal{K}$. Hence, (14) can be expressed in its simple form as $E_d(t)=\\frac{\\sum_{n=1}^{K}s_{n,d}(t)}{\\alpha_d}-\\frac{(p_l-p_d(t))K}{k\\alpha_d}$ (15)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E29","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"W. Tushar, et al. coalition can be expressed by (2 L L m = 1 (bm , c ( t ) sm, c ( t )) ( pl + pc ( ","equation_id":"16-17","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Similarly, total amount of energy received by the receivers of the coalition can be expressed by $E_c(t)=\\sum_{m=1}^{L}e_{m,c}(t)=\\sum_{m=1}^{L}\\left(\\frac{b_{m,c}(t)-s_{m,c}(t)}{\\alpha_c}-\\frac{p_l+p_c(t)}{k\\alpha_c}\\right)$ (16), assuming $\\alpha_{m,c}=\\alpha_c, \\forall m\\in\\mathcal{L}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E33","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"prosumer needs to pay the government tax and a subscription fee, ca captured via , for using the tra","equation_id":"18-19","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"$p_{c,s2}(t)=\\frac{p_l(\\alpha_c K-\\alpha_d L)-k\\left(\\alpha_c\\sum_{n=1}^{K}s_{n,d}(t)-\\alpha_d\\sum_{m=1}^{L}(b_{m,c}(t)-s_{m,c}(t))\\right)}{\\alpha_c K+\\alpha_d(1+\\beta)L}(1+\\beta)$ (19). Thus, $p_{d,s2}(t)$ and $p_{c,s2}(t)$ are the discharging and charging prices used by prosumers at state 2 to trade their battery energy over the P2P network."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E32","quote":"To this end, by equating (15) and (16) and replacing the value of $p_c(t)$ with $p_d(t)$ from (17), the trading prices $p_c(t)$ and $p_d(t)$ for prosumers at state 2 can be calculated as:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E31","quote":"the total energy charged by the receivers batteries should be equal to the total energy discharged by the providers"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","quote":"The relationship in (17) is motivated by the fact that a prosumer needs to pay the government tax and a subscription fee, captured via $\\beta$, for using the transmission line provide by the grid for P2P purpose."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","quote":"1: for time slot $t=1$ to $T$ do 2: Set P2P discharge price $p_d(t)=\\frac{p_b(t)+p_s(t)}{2}$. 3: Set P2P charge price $p_c(t)=(1+\\beta)p_d(t)$."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","quote":"when a prosumer may want its battery to be charged or discharged for trading in the peer-to-peer market, the trading price should reflect the associated battery degradation cost due to charging and discharging, and at the same time, have enough incentive to make the price beneficial for prosumers to put their batteries into the market."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"bb10cf8133e16866237a475727bc71b1dc6bf1ff3c7afdf907cfd6dfe5ef4af6","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source gives explicit pricing equations for this rule: local state-2 battery-energy balance E_d(t)=E_c(t), the derived discharging price (18), the charging/discharging relation (17), and Algorithm 1's initial setting p_d(t)=(p_b(t)+p_s(t))/2 and p_c(t)=(1+β)p_d(t). These are formalized at pricing.local with the existing clearing.local -> pricing.local and settlement.payment -> pricing.local edges. Constraint C004 is qualitative and remains not_formalized. B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x-Ed","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"E_d(t) is aggregate provider discharge entering the local clearing balance that links clearing.local to pricing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x-Ec","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"E_c(t) is aggregate receiver charge entering the local clearing balance that links clearing.local to pricing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pd","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_d(t) is set at pricing.local in Algorithm 1's initial price-setting step."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pc","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_c(t) is set at pricing.local in Algorithm 1's initial price-setting step."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pd-s2","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"p_{d,s2}(t) is the state-2 price calculated from the clearing balance represented by the clearing.local -> pricing.local edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x-pc-s2","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"p_{c,s2}(t) is the state-2 charging price derived from the same balance-based state-2 discharging price."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-pb","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_b(t) is an exogenous mid-market buying-price input at pricing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-ps","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_s(t) is an exogenous mid-market selling-price input at pricing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-beta","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001","v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"β appears in the state-2 price expression and in the settlement-related charging/discharging price markup; edge E002 records the settlement.payment -> pricing.local relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-pl","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"p_l is the battery degradation cost entering the state-2 price expression under the clearing-to-pricing relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-alpha-c","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"α_c is the common receiver satisfaction parameter in the state-2 price expression."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-alpha-d","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"α_d is the common provider satisfaction parameter in the state-2 price expression."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-k","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"k is the utility scaling factor appearing in the state-2 price expression."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-K","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"K is the provider count in the state-2 balance and price expression."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-L","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"L is the receiver count in the state-2 balance and price expression."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-s-n-d","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"s_{n,d}(t) is a summed provider battery-state symbol in the state-2 price expression; its separate definition is unresolved."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-b-m-c","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"b_{m,c}(t) is a summed receiver battery-capacity/state symbol in the state-2 price expression; its separate definition is unresolved."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-s-m-c","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"s_{m,c}(t) is a summed receiver battery-state symbol in the state-2 price expression; its separate definition is unresolved."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E001"],"rationale":"C001 formalizes the local aggregate battery-energy balance and resulting state-2 price expression that the frozen edge clearing.local -> pricing.local represents."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R007-E002"],"rationale":"C002 formalizes the β markup relation linking tax/subscription-fee settlement considerations at settlement.payment to the charging/discharging price at pricing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 formalizes Algorithm 1's initial price-setting step entirely at pricing.local."}],"revision_requests":["B re-extraction should define or otherwise confirm the symbols s_{n,d}(t), b_{m,c}(t), and s_{m,c}(t) used in Eq. (18); the supplied pages do not give separate definitions for them.","Resolve the inconsistent placement of (1+β) in Eq. (19) across v141-b-g02-E33 and v141-b-g03-E04; this patch uses p_{c,s2}(t)=(1+β)p_{d,s2}(t), consistent with Eq. (17) and v141-b-g02-E33, and does not formalize the divided variant.","Confirm whether Algorithm 1's p_d(t)/p_c(t) and the state-2 p_{d,s2}(t)/p_{c,s2}(t) are intended as the same or distinct price objects; this patch retains distinct symbols because the supplied source uses distinct notation.","No graph revision is requested for V/E: the existing nodes clearing.local, pricing.local and settlement.payment and the two frozen edges are sufficient for the supported expressions."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
